{"repositoryId":1323230136,"availability":"available","full":"SamGabriel-Here/celestial","name":"celestial","description":"A cinematic weather app that renders the sky your city is actually under — live conditions, hourly curve, 5-day forecast, air quality, daylight and moon phase. React, TypeScript and Vite on Vercel.","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-08-04T17:51:39Z","updated":"2026-10-14T15:44:58Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://celestialsky.vercel.app","topics":["canvas","dataviz","frontend","openweather","openweathermap-api","react","serverless","typescript","vercel","vite","weather","weather-app"],"demo":"https://celestialsky.vercel.app/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T02:48:51.392Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T02:48:51.392Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T02:48:51.392Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-19T02:48:51.392Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The real sky over any place, on a star wheel you turn.","Celestial is a weather app built like a planisphere. In the middle is a round window onto the sky over the place you searched — the sun, the moon at its actual phase, the brightest stars where they really are, today's sun path, and the cloud and rain the forecast expects. Around it is a printed rim. Turn it, and the window shows the sky at that moment.","Nothing in the window is decoration. Every position is computed from the date and the coordinates; every veil of cloud and streak of rain is that hour's forecast."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/SamGabriel-Here/celestial/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"01dc89accfd0d970883c60a821e9c8c2e2ee213ad8f483a8f71e36d6b7b8fe64","extractedAt":"2026-10-19T02:48:51.477Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T02:48:51.477Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"The real sky over any place, on a star wheel you turn.","sourceUrl":"http